@startuml ICNNA_v2_0_0_spine_classes
' ============================================================
' ICNNA v2.0.0 — Projected spine class diagram
' Scope: +icnna/+data/+core  (flat, relationsManager-mediated)
' Companion diagrams (planned): snirf, ops, qc, io/devices
' Phase 3b deliverable
' ============================================================
' Log:
'   2026-04-15: FOE/Claude — File created from roadmap.
'   2026-04-21: FOE/Claude — Major revision per FOE review:
'       + Three-tier certainty styling (existing/planned/speculative)
'       + Added document class (speculative, D.new.5)
'       + Added experiment class (speculative, from package notes)
'       + Added structuredData class (planned, central 3D tensor)
'       + Added device class (speculative, replaces legacy dataSource)
'       + Added level class (planned, from Cantor hub_level)
'       + Added treatment class (speculative, from Cantor hub_treatment)
'       + Added mechanism class (speculative, from Cantor hub_mechanism)
'       + Added sessionDefinition class (speculative, template pattern)
'       + Added deviceDefinition class (speculative, template pattern;
'         renamed from dataSourceDefinition per FOE)
'       + Upgraded session to planned tier (D.new.6)
'       + Enriched factor with factorType from Cantor
'       + qcCriterion marked abstract (concrete subclasses to +qc)
'       + experiment gains unitIDs (within/between determination)
'       + document gains bundleIDs, pipelineIDs
'       + experimentBundle gains experimentIDs (provenance)
'       + session gains deviceIDs
'       + metaEntry aggregation to identifiableObject added
'       + Note on ternary relation concern (experiment-group-unit)
'       + Scoped to +data/+core only (Option B split)
'   2026-04-21 (r2): FOE/Claude — Second revision:
'       + Added structuredData (planned, central 3D tensor)
'       + Added device (speculative, replaces legacy dataSource)
'       + Renamed dataSourceDefinition -> deviceDefinition
'       + Updated ID references and notes
'       + 31 classes total (20 existing + 5 planned + 6 speculative)
'   2026-05-04: FOE/Claude — Fresh-eyes review corrections:
'       + experiment promoted from speculative to planned
'       + rawData and montage restored to abstract
'       + factorIDs added to experimentBundle class body
'       + run class added (speculative, from Cantor hub_run)
'       + experimentDesign class added (speculative, extracted
'         from experiment.designType struct)
'       + experiment gains bundleIDs (bidirectional link with
'         experimentBundle)
'       + session gains runIDs
'       + subject inheritance fixed: subject --|> experimentalUnit
'       + identifiableObject retains name alongside description
'       + 34 classes total (20 existing + 6 planned + 8 speculative)
'       + N-ary relation concern elevated to pre-Phase-4 task
'   2026-06-16: FOE/Claude — relationsManager architecture
'       (Phase 3b continuation 6, Item E resolution):
'       + Added relationsManager class (planned) — singleton
'         value class implementing a typed, role-labeled
'         hypergraph for all entity relations.
'       + identifiableObject gains relationsManagerID property.
'       + ALL *IDs reference properties removed from entity
'         classes (~40 properties eliminated). Entity classes
'         now hold only intrinsic attributes.
'       + ALL inter-entity ID-reference arrows removed.
'         Relations managed exclusively via the hypergraph.
'       + 1:1 compositional references (e.g. structuredData
'         to timeline) become derived properties that query
'         the manager — transparent to the user.
'       + Centralised ID uniqueness enforcement in the manager.
'       + N-ary relation concern (Item E) RESOLVED.
'       + 35 classes total (20 existing + 7 planned +
'         8 speculative).
' ============================================================
' Source: Phase3_minute.tex roadmap, Phase2c v2.0.0 endpoint,
'         D.* decisions, Cantor cantor.sql schema,
'         legacy oo/@structuredData, legacy oo/@dataSource,
'         20-Apr-2026 package diagram, 21-Apr-2026 FOE review,
'         04-May-2026 fresh-eyes review,
'         16-Jun-2026 relationsManager decision (Item E).
' ============================================================
' Conventions:
'   - "Flat + relationsManager-mediated" (P5 evolved):
'     entities hold only intrinsic attributes; all
'     inter-entity relations live in the relationsManager's
'     typed hypergraph. Entities access related entities via
'     derived properties that query the manager.
'   - Three-tier certainty:
'       Normal border     = exists in v1.4.1-beta
'       <<planned>>       = committed in roadmap (bold blue)
'       <<speculative>>   = likely but not committed (dashed gray)
'   - SPECULATIVE classes to be revised at implementation memos.
' ============================================================

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 30

' --- Tier styling via stereotypes ---
skinparam class<<planned>> {
  BorderColor DarkBlue
  BorderThickness 2
  FontStyle bold
}
skinparam class<<speculative>> {
  BorderColor Gray
  BorderStyle dashed
  FontStyle italic
}

title ICNNA v2.0.0 — Projected Core Spine Classes (+data/+core)\n35 classes: 20 existing | 7 planned | 8 speculative\nExisting (normal) | Planned (bold blue) | Speculative (dashed gray)\nAll inter-entity relations managed by relationsManager (hypergraph)

package "+icnna.data.core (v2.0.0)" as core {

  ' ================================================================
  ' ROOT
  ' ================================================================
  abstract class identifiableObject {
    +id : char
    +name : char
    +description : char
    +created : datetime
    +modified : datetime
    +classVersion : char
    +relationsManagerID : char
  }

  class metaEntry {
    +key : char
    +value : any
  }

  ' ================================================================
  ' RELATIONS MANAGER (Phase 3b cont. 6, Item E)
  ' ================================================================
  class relationsManager <<planned>> {
    +typeRegistry : containers.Map
    +tuples : cell
  }

  ' ================================================================
  ' TOP-LEVEL CONTAINER
  ' ================================================================
  class document <<speculative>> {
  }

  ' ================================================================
  ' EXPERIMENT AND DESIGN
  ' ================================================================
  class experiment <<planned>> {
  }

  class experimentDesign <<speculative>> {
    +experimentType : enum
    +temporalDesign : enum
    +subjectDesign : enum
    +factorialType : enum
    +replicationStrategy : char
  }

  class experimentBundle {
    +designKind : enum
  }

  class experimentalGroup {
  }

  class experimentalUnit {
  }

  class subject {
    +demographics : struct
  }

  ' ================================================================
  ' SESSION LAYER
  ' ================================================================
  class session <<planned>> {
    +date : datetime
  }

  class sessionDefinition <<speculative>> {
    +protocol : char
  }

  class run <<speculative>> {
    +runNumber : int
  }

  ' ================================================================
  ' DEVICE LAYER (replaces legacy dataSource / dataSourceDefinition)
  ' ================================================================
  class device <<speculative>> {
    +deviceNumber : int
  }

  class deviceDefinition <<speculative>> {
    +deviceKind : char
  }

  ' ================================================================
  ' DATA LAYER
  ' ================================================================
  class structuredData <<planned>> {
    +data : double[3D]
    +signalTags : cell
  }

  abstract class rawData {
    +deviceKind : char
  }

  ' ================================================================
  ' EXPERIMENTAL DESIGN FACTORS
  ' ================================================================
  class factor <<planned>> {
    +kind : enum
    +factorType : enum
  }

  class level <<planned>> {
    +label : char
    +ordinal : int
  }

  class treatment <<speculative>> {
  }

  class mechanism <<speculative>> {
    +mechanismType : enum
  }

  class condition {
    +label : char
  }

  ' ================================================================
  ' TIMELINE / EVENTS
  ' ================================================================
  class timeline {
    +tStart : datetime
    +nominalFs : double
  }

  class event <<planned>> {
    +tOnset : double
    +tDuration : double
  }

  ' ================================================================
  ' SIGNAL DESCRIPTION
  ' ================================================================
  class signalSet {
  }

  class signalDescriptor {
    +modality : enum
    +unit : char
  }

  ' ================================================================
  ' OPTICAL HARDWARE
  ' ================================================================
  abstract class montage

  class nirsMontage {
  }

  class optode {
    +position : double[3]
  }

  class lightSource

  class lightDetector

  class referenceLocation {
    +label : char
    +position : double[3]
  }

  class opticalCoefficient

  ' ================================================================
  ' QUALITY CONTROL (abstract contracts; concrete subclasses in +qc)
  ' ================================================================
  class qc {
  }

  abstract class qcCriterion {
    +tier : enum
    +parameters : struct
  }
}

' ================================================================
' INHERITANCE
' ================================================================
' --- Existing classes ---
experimentBundle     --|> identifiableObject
experimentalGroup    --|> identifiableObject
experimentalUnit     --|> identifiableObject
subject              --|> experimentalUnit
condition            --|> identifiableObject
timeline             --|> identifiableObject
rawData              --|> identifiableObject
signalSet            --|> identifiableObject
signalDescriptor     --|> identifiableObject
montage              --|> identifiableObject
nirsMontage          --|> montage
optode               --|> identifiableObject
lightSource          --|> optode
lightDetector        --|> optode
referenceLocation    --|> identifiableObject
opticalCoefficient   --|> identifiableObject
qc                   --|> identifiableObject
qcCriterion          --|> identifiableObject

' --- Planned classes ---
session              --|> identifiableObject
structuredData       --|> identifiableObject
factor               --|> identifiableObject
level                --|> identifiableObject
event                --|> identifiableObject
experiment           --|> identifiableObject
relationsManager     --|> identifiableObject

' --- Speculative classes ---
document             --|> identifiableObject
experimentDesign     --|> identifiableObject
sessionDefinition    --|> identifiableObject
run                  --|> identifiableObject
deviceDefinition     --|> identifiableObject
device               --|> identifiableObject
treatment            --|> identifiableObject
mechanism            --|> identifiableObject

' ================================================================
' AGGREGATION
' ================================================================
identifiableObject   o-- "0..*" metaEntry : meta

' ================================================================
' RELATIONS MANAGER LINK
' ================================================================
identifiableObject   ..> relationsManager : relationsManagerID

' ================================================================
' NOTES
' ================================================================

note top of relationsManager
  **PLANNED** — Singleton value class.
  Typed, role-labeled hypergraph.
  ..
  All inter-entity relations stored as
  generic tuples: (type, {role->ID, ...}).
  Entities hold no relationship state;
  derived properties query the manager.
  ..
  **Registered relation categories:**
  Experimental design: membership,
    factorAllocation, conditionMapping,
    treatmentAssignment, mechanism, design.
  Data acquisition: unitSession,
    acquisition, production, runs, timelines.
  Composition (~15): 1:1 bindings surfaced
    as derived properties on entities.
  Template/Definition links.
  Analysis/Bundle provenance.
  Document-level containment.
  ~35 types. Open-ended by design.
  ..
  **Centralised services:**
  ID uniqueness enforcement (per type).
  Schema validation (assertInvariants).
  Cascade removal (removeEntity).
  ..
  Singleton via persistent variable
  (value class, no handles).
  Pure value data; serialises natively.
end note

note top of document
  **SPECULATIVE** — Top-level container.
  v2.0.0: single experiment.
  Post-v2.0.0: multi-experiment
  (meta-analysis).
  Hosts experiments, bundles, and
  pipelines via relationsManager.
end note

note top of experiment
  **PLANNED** — Expanded from legacy
  @experiment. Participates in relations
  for groups, units, bundles, sessions,
  devices, and experimental design
  — all via relationsManager.
  ..
  Within/between-subject determination
  via manager query on membership
  relation (experiment, group, unit).
  ..
  Bidirectional experiment-bundle link
  stored as hypergraph tuples (both
  directions are queries, not storage).
  ..
  All former *IDs properties removed;
  accessed via derived properties
  that query the relationsManager.
end note

note bottom of experimentDesign
  **SPECULATIVE** — Extracted from
  experiment.designType struct.
  Captures experimental design taxonomy:
    experimentType (experiment /
      pseudo / quasi),
    temporalDesign (cross-sectional /
      longitudinal),
    subjectDesign (within / between / mixed),
    factorialType (full / nested / incomplete),
    replicationStrategy.
  ..
  Likely to become its own class when
  validation logic is needed.
end note

note right of experimentBundle
  GENERALISED at v1.4.7:
  - block, event-related, mixed designs
  - within-group allocation (factor)
  - multifactorial designs (factor[*])
  ..
  Analytical dataframe: can span 1+
  experiments. Relations to experiments,
  groups, and factors managed via the
  relationsManager.
end note

note right of structuredData
  **PLANNED** — Central data container.
  3D tensor: samples x channels x signals.
  Replaces legacy oo/@structuredData.
  ..
  Compositional links (timeline, signalSet,
  qc, montage) are derived properties
  querying the relationsManager.
  ..
  Subclasses (in companion diagrams):
  neuroimage, ecg, physiologicalMeasurement,
  etc.
  ..
  Lazy-proxy candidate (D.new.7):
  data array loaded on demand.
end note

note bottom of device
  **SPECULATIVE** — Replaces legacy
  oo/@dataSource. Intermediary between
  session and raw/structured data.
  Each device instance corresponds to
  one data acquisition device in a session.
  Relations managed via relationsManager.
end note

note bottom of run
  **SPECULATIVE** — From Cantor hub_run.
  A run is a temporal subdivision of a
  session (e.g. multiple recordings within
  a single session visit). Each run has
  its own timeline (via relationsManager).
end note

note bottom of sessionDefinition
  **Naming TBD**: "*Definition" follows
  legacy convention. Alternatives:
  *Template, *Spec, *Contract.
  ..
  Pattern: Definition = template/contract;
  session / device = instance. Enables
  compliance checking and filtering.
  deviceDefinition follows same pattern.
end note

note right of treatment
  From Cantor schema (hub_treatment).
  A treatment is a specific combination
  of factor levels applied to units.
  Relations (treatment-level, unit-treatment)
  managed via relationsManager.
end note

note bottom of mechanism
  From Cantor schema (hub_mechanism).
  Experimental design mechanisms:
  blinding, blocking, randomization.
  Linked per experiment via relationsManager.
end note

note right of factor
  kind: allocation (within / between / mixed).
  factorType: role (treatment / cofactor /
  confounder) — from Cantor hub_factor.
end note

note as resolvedNote #CCFFCC
  **RESOLVED — N-ary relation management**
  (FOE, 16-Jun-2026, Item E):
  ..
  Architecture: typed, role-labeled
  hypergraph (generic tuples) wrapped
  in a schema-validating singleton
  value class (assertInvariants pattern).
  ..
  Key outcomes:
  - ~40 *IDs properties eliminated
    from entity classes.
  - Entities hold only intrinsic attributes.
  - 1:1 compositions surfaced as derived
    properties (transparent to user).
  - Centralised ID uniqueness and
    schema validation.
  - Singleton value class (no handles).
  - Open-ended: new relation types
    registered, not hard-coded.
  ..
  **Item E closed.**
end note

note bottom of core
  **Flat + relationsManager-mediated**
  (P5 evolved, 16-Jun-2026):
  Entities hold only intrinsic attributes.
  All inter-entity relations (n-ary,
  bidirectional, compositional) live in
  the relationsManager hypergraph.
  Derived properties on entities provide
  transparent access to related entities.
  ..
  **Lazy-proxy pattern** (<<planned>>,
  cross-cutting, D.new.7):
  Data containers load arrays on demand,
  not at construction time. Applies to:
  structuredData, rawData, signalSet,
  timeline, dataBlock, etc.
  ..
  **QC migration** (D.new.8):
  Abstract qc / qcCriterion contracts stay
  in +core. Concrete subclasses move to +qc:
  _Saturation, _Mirroring, _ChannelIntegrity
  (v1.5.4 survival tier);
  _SCI, _CV (v1.6.4 enhancement tier).
  See companion +qc diagram.
  ..
  **Companion diagrams** (Option B):
  - +data/+snirf (8 classes, largely unchanged)
  - +op/* classes (proc, stats, pipeline)
  - +qc concrete subclasses
  - +io/+devices importers (rawData_NIRx etc.)
  ..
  Method-level surface deferred to
  implementation memos (v1.4.7b onward).
end note

@enduml
